## Timeline: Sequential vs Swarm

### Sequential (Current)

```
Analysis:        10 min  (1 instance)
Inventory:       15 min  (1 instance)
Domain:          15 min  (1 instance)
Boundaries:      2 hours (human decision)
──────────────────────
Loop 34 services:
  Service 1:     40 min (extract + verify + harden)
  Service 2:     40 min
  ...
  Service 34:    40 min
──────────────────────
  + Manual cutover: 27 hours per service (soak)

Total: 1,360 hours = 56 days
```

### Swarm Parallel (New)

```
Analysis:        10 min  (1 instance)
Inventory:       15 min  (1 instance, can start after analysis)
Domain:          15 min  (1 instance, can start after analysis)
Boundaries:      2 hours (human decision)
──────────────────────
Extraction Phase:
  4 services in parallel:
    Service 1-4: 40 min each
    Total time:  40 min (not 160 min)

Verification Phase:
  6 services in parallel:
    Service 1-6: 40 min each
    Total time:  40 min (not 240 min)

Hardening Phase:
  6 services in parallel:
    Service 1-6: 40 min each
    Total time:  40 min (not 240 min)

Loop continues for all 34 services
  Total extraction+verify+harden: ~4 hours (not 1,300 hours)

──────────────────────
+ Manual cutover: 27 hours per service (soak) - SEQUENTIAL by environment
  But can run 3-4 services in parallel across dev/staging/prod environments
  Real time: ~7 days (with 3 parallel environments)

Total: Analysis (40 min) + Extraction (4 hours) + Manual (7 days) = ~7 days
```

**Result: 56 days → 7 days (8x faster)**

